+# Feature Specification: Long-Stay Discount
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Draft
+
+**Input**: A rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price. Quotes and bookings both show the reduced total.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Reduced price for long rentals (P1)
+Desk staff quote and book rentals; customers staying 3 days or more pay 10% less.
+**Acceptance**:
+1. Given a board at 2500 cents/day, when quoting 3 days, then total is 6750 (full price 7500 less 10%).
+2. Given the same board, when quoting 2 days, then total is 5000 (no discount).
+3. Given a rental of 3+ days, booking returns a total equal to the quote.
+4. Given a full price whose 10% reduction is not a whole number of cents, the total is rounded half up to integer cents.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: Full price = days × dailyPrice. If days ≥ 3, total = full price less 10%, rounded half up to integer cents; otherwise total = full price.
+- **FR-002**: `quote` and `book` apply the same rule, so a booking's total always equals the quote for the same request.
+- **FR-003**: No other fields or behaviour (availability, overlap, validation) change.
+
+## Assumptions
+- The discount depends only on rental length in whole days, not on item kind or customer.
+- Discount is a flat 10% of the whole rental (not only of days beyond the second).
+
+## Success Criteria
+- All acceptance scenarios pass as automated tests, and existing tests remain valid except where they expected full price for 3+ days.
